# The medallion store. `docs/medallion.md` describes the layout; what is versioned here and
# what is not follows from which layers can be re-derived.
#
# Landing and bronze are the record of what was observed: nothing derives them, so they are
# kept, and git is what makes a deletion recoverable.

# Derived wholesale from bronze, in seconds, by `just sessionise` and `just ingest-motis`.
/silver/

# Gold is derived too, and ignored but for what a build reads rather than a query: the
# crossings a device carries in flash and a browser fetches, and the sessions a kiosk replays.
# Neither can be re-derived by whoever builds — a checkout has no silver to derive them from —
# so they are versioned alongside the code. Every version packed is kept, and
# `crossings.version` and `sessions.version` name the ones in use.
/gold/*
!/gold/artifact=crossings/
!/gold/artifact=sessions/

# Point-in-time extracts of Overture: 1.5 GB, and re-derivable — `bronze/extract_manifest`
# records the release and window each one took, and an Overture release never changes.
/bronze/overture_extract/
